=2 Walkthrough
* Speak to {n:Waoud} - (J-10) top floor.
* He will offer to give you a divination and will ask the following questions.
* Upon success, {n:Waoud} will mention seeing all five serpent symbols.
** It is possible to not be able to progress further in the quest, as he may mention only one serpent.
*** If you cannot progress, you will have the option to try again the next game day.
* Below is a listing of the questions and answers. The answers in bold are a combination of answers that have worked for some.
** Others report answering the third option for each question works as well.

|^Question|Answer 1|Answer 2|Answer 3
|What is destiny? Destiny is something that...|Is immutable.|~h~One forges for oneself.|Is unknowable.
|Does the accomplishment of a goal require sacrifice and hardship? {br}Do goals require sacrifice?|Not if you think hard enough.|Occasionally.|~h~Absolutely.
|You hold in your hands a forbidden scroll. {br}Reading it will bring you untold wisdom, but cost all that you own. Do you...|Read the scroll?|Throw the scroll away?|~h~Burn the scroll?
|If the loss of one life would save ten thousand, would you offer yourself without hesitation?|Offer yourself?|Offer another... {br}I have no such courage.|~h~Without hesitation.
|Would you choose a tumultuous life where fame or fortune were attainable, or a tranquil life where both were forever beyond your reach? {br}Which do you choose?|~h~A chaotic life.|A tranquil life.|A mix of both.
|You stand on the precipice between life and death. Would you choose to live life as a beast if it would save you from falling into the shadowy abyss of the underworld? What do you do?|If it keeps me from dying...|Fall, and keep my humanity.|~h~Embrace life as a beast.
|A companion in battle turns against you, raising a weapon to attack. {br}Do you...|Brace for the blow?|Try to reason with him?|~h~Cut him down?
|A loved one is afflicted with a terrible illness and has little time left to live. {br}You are asked to end that life by your own hand. Do you...|Seek a cure?|Leave the world together?|~h~Grant the request?
|You are in the midst of a fierce battle. {br}The enemy lying at your feet was once a friend. His breath is ragged and weak. Do you...|Tend to his wounds?|~h~End his pain?|Ignore your old friend?
|A superior to whom you owe a great debt orders you to act in a way that violates your sense of justice. Do you...|Try to remove him from power?|Carry out the order?|~h~Follow your sense of justice?

* Right after answering all his questions, Waoud will tell you which kind of treasure he's interested in, but you won't be able to progress until the **next Vana'diel day** and until you zone at least once.
* When Waoud asks for the treasure, he will use the following clues **(Make sure you read the item entries themselves for important info!)**:

* "The treasure I would have you seek is a pinch of golden sand. It is said to glow with the light of the sun and be found only on a certain beach."
** {@i:Sunsand|503} {i:Sunsand|Sunsand|503}, {z:Valkurm Dunes} (H-9) Only spawns during dust storms.
** This is the only requested item that can be purchased at the {z:Auction House} ({@g:Auction House} > Other > Misc.)

* "The treasure I would have you seek is a jewel. It is said to glow with a bluish tint and be found near the bank of a certain river."
** **Unequip your Main and Sub weapons in order to pick this item up!**
** {@i:Siren's Tear|576} {i:Siren's Tear|Siren's Tear|576}, {z:North Gustaberg} near (J-9) along the river, use tab button to seek out the blank spot. (Appears as a ???)
*** {z:Port Bastok} {p:homepoint|Homepoint} exit is closest.

* "The treasure I would have you seek is a precious stone. It is said to be as red as blood and found in a land of geysers."
** {@i:Dangruf Stone|553} {i:Dangruf Stone|Dangruf Stone|553}, {z:Dangruf Wadi} (I/J-5)

* Trade him the item and he will tell you to go to {z:Aydeewa Subterrane}.
** Keep the requested item in your inventory. You won't get the next cutscene at the pond if you don't have the item on you.
* Enter Aydeewa Subterrane at (G-7) in {z:Bhaflau Thickets}, and proceed to the platform at (H-9) for a cutscene. During the cutscene, choose to take his hand to continue.
** The {p:Voidwatch|VW} warp is the fastest shortcut to this location.
** Make sure to take his hand. If you refuse him every time instead, the entire quest will reset and you'll have to start over from the beginning.

* When the cutscene is over, you will be returned to Aht Urhgan Whitegate and be able to change to Blue Mage.
** The item you brought will still be in your inventory afterwards. At this point you're free to use it on another quest, throw it out, etc.
* You can return to {n:Waoud} and ask him to "gaze away" at your fate to get a cutscene. This is necessary for the next quest.

